from pathlib import Path
r=Path.cwd()
p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');new='''USER.append(('Compare screen history and visual changes', [
'Open the intended saved project, then choose Screen history in the upper-right page selector. Import actual PNG evidence on Screenshots first: enter a named contributor and a caption describing the screen, application build and conditions, then click Import screenshot. Each image belongs to the generation displayed at import. Import the earlier image while its matching generation is current; after reassessment import the later image. A caption does not verify an image against source.',
'Select the Before and After screenshot records by artifact ID, generation and caption. The newest 200 imports are available. Choose Imported images and click Compare. Scroll the command bar horizontally to reach hidden commands. Scroll the page vertically to see the previews, change list and evidence memo. Swap sides exchanges both images and form paths; click Compare again. Changing a selection clears the previous result and discards a late worker response.',
'The pixel mask uses top-left coordinates and compares exact decoded RGB after transparency is composited on white. Red marks changed overlapping pixels; magenta marks an extent present on only one side; white means unchanged or outside both. The evidence memo reports counts, inclusive changed bounds, original dimensions, contributors, import times, generation IDs and SHA256 fingerprints. Images are fitted only for display; comparison does not resize, align, normalize color profiles or apply a tolerance. Animation, theme, DPI and content changes can affect pixels without proving a defect or its cause.',
'For captured layouts enter both relative form paths, for example forms/Main.dfm, before clicking Compare. Choose Captured layouts to see blue Before geometry, orange After geometry and their overlay. Both retained captures must use the same project and analysis selection with compatible parser contracts. These drawings are approximate reconstructions, not runtime screenshots. They omit style/custom-paint behavior and show at most 300 component rectangles per pane. Missing property values remain unknown, default or inherited.',
'Filter the layout change list by component path or serialized values. First page and Next page show 250 rows at a time. Select a row to read added, removed or changed classes/properties and their exact before/after evidence. Renames appear as removal plus addition. Missing historical captures or form paths produce an explicit layout gap while keeping the valid image comparison. Keep necessary releases through Database tools before retention removes a capture. Full executable paths, practice steps and test commands are in docs/guides/Screen_History_Run_and_Test.txt.'
]))
ENGINEERING.append(('Compare attributed screen evidence and captured layouts', [
'DPH.Workspace.ScreenHistory verifies managed PNG bytes against their saved image hashes, bounds each image and the union canvas to 16 million pixels with dimensions no greater than 8192 and encoded size no greater than 20 MiB, then decodes with the VCL PNG library on the worker. CPU bitmaps composite transparency on white and compare exact eight-bit RGB. No target form, class or executable is loaded. The report preserves image and metadata hashes, contributors, generation IDs, dimensions, counts and inclusive bounds; private managed paths are omitted.',
'The screen_history worker command resolves screenshot IDs through the existing checksum-validated store. Optional layout comparison loads each image generation from its retained workspace cache. Missing or incompatible layout evidence yields layout_gap without discarding verified images. Parent-local component paths match captured classes and sorted inspector properties; duplicate identities are refused. Source offsets alone do not count as a change. Comparison supports 5000 components per form; all changes remain in the paged list, while previews draw at most 300 rectangles per side.',
'DPH.UI.Main.fmx serializes the Screen history page, grid, image and paint controls, selectors, toolbar and details. Panels use client alignment in their grid cells. Source geometry is fitted on a common canvas in blue and orange. Request tokens plus the database identity prevent a late response from restoring evidence after a pair or path change. Processing and PNG comparison run in the existing worker; presentation uses FMX. No storage migration, runtime control construction or source mutation is required.',
'Run tools/build-screen-history.cmd elevated for 73 checks covering exact pixels/bounds, transparency, size changes, altered bytes, union limits, text and binary DFM, FMX, parser/selection incompatibility, persisted image attribution, missing retained captures, native Compare, late-response rejection, pagination/filtering, swap, visible geometry and compact layout. Fixtures reuse bin/screen-history-validation. The owner catalog is restored after exercising cached open. Native PaintTo renders show actual DPH controls; controlled synthetic images do not establish target-runtime observations.'
]))
for chapters in (USER, ENGINEERING):
    for index, (heading, paragraphs) in enumerate(chapters):
        chapters[index] = (heading, [p.replace('337 requirement records remain incomplete', '336 requirement records remain incomplete') for p in paragraphs])

'''
assert 'Compare screen history and visual changes' not in s;s=s.replace('user_order = [',new+'user_order = [',1).replace("'Import actual screenshot evidence',","'Import actual screenshot evidence', 'Compare screen history and visual changes',",1).replace("'guide_version': 14","'guide_version': 15");p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=r/'README.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s+='''
Choose **Screen history** to compare two attributed screenshot records. Click
**Compare** for side-by-side images, an exact pixel mask and counts. Enter both
relative DFM/FMX paths for captured component/property differences and a layout
overlay. Imported images and approximate reconstructions retain distinct labels.
Scroll the command bar sideways and the page down for commands and evidence.
[Explicit run and test directions](docs/guides/Screen_History_Run_and_Test.txt)
cover import generations, pixel colors, retention and limitations. Run
`tools\\build-screen-history.cmd` elevated for 73 focused checks.
''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=r/'help/index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');section='''<section><h2>Compare screen history and visual changes</h2><p>Open the intended saved project. On <strong>Screenshots</strong> enter a named contributor and descriptive caption, then import a PNG while its matching source generation is current. Import the later image after capturing the later source. These are contributor images, not automatically verified runtime evidence.</p><p>Choose <strong>Screen history</strong> in the upper-right page selector. Select Before and After by ID, generation and caption; choose <strong>Imported images</strong> and click <strong>Compare</strong>. Scroll the command bar horizontally and the page vertically to reach hidden controls and evidence. Red pixels changed in the overlap; magenta marks extent on only one side. Counts and inclusive bounds appear in the evidence memo, together with contributors and image/metadata hashes. Exact RGB is compared after transparency is composited on white; no automatic alignment, resizing or tolerance is applied.</p><p>For layout comparison, enter both relative DFM/FMX paths before Compare, then choose <strong>Captured layouts</strong>. Blue is Before and orange is After; the third pane overlays them. These are approximate source reconstructions, not runtime screenshots. Select a change row to read exact old/new properties. Filter by text and use First page/Next page for 250 rows at a time. Missing retained captures or forms produce an explicit layout gap without invalidating the images. Use Database tools to retain important generations. Swap sides exchanges image choices and paths; click Compare again. Changed selections clear stale results.</p><p>The page lists the newest 200 imports. Comparisons support PNG files up to 20 MiB, dimensions up to 8192 and 16 million pixels per image and union. Layout comparison supports 5000 components per form; previews show at most 300 rectangles per side. Full steps: <code>docs/guides/Screen_History_Run_and_Test.txt</code>. Developer checks: <code>tools/build-screen-history.cmd</code>, elevated.</p></section>'''
marker='<section><h2>Record user actions and business purposes</h2>';assert marker in s;s=s.replace(marker,section+marker,1);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=r/'bin/verify-screen-history-guides.py';s=(r/'bin/verify-action-purposes-guides.py').read_text().replace("==14","==15").replace('Record user actions and business purposes','Compare screen history and visual changes').replace('Store attributed action purpose mappings','Compare attributed screen evidence and captured layouts').replace('action-purposes-guide-check.json','screen-history-guide-check.json');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
